Z||000000||Little Duce Coupe||12-20-2001||11:43 AM||||<BR>The best and easiest way to make your Iron Duke as fast as youve ever wanted is to....<P>Drive it the morning your POS! Ford250 (that you just bought last summer in order to keep the miles off your treasured Fiero) WONT START.. AGAIN ARGHHHHHHHHH!!!!@#$(&%@(%.<P>#($ D#@(*$ pos, in the summer it ran fine, now that it turns cold it won't.<BR>Dead cold it will start, but somewhere in between cold and hot...if I let it die it just craps out and won't start.  Starter fluid don't do it, pumping the pedal don't do it, flooring the pedal don't do it only leaving it sit for a long time seems to do anything.<P>The only upside is that after driving this 8mpg behemouth for a few months MAN is the Ole Iron Duke a screamer!<BR>I forgot how much fun and how comfy on a cold morning it is to drive.<P>Guess the Ford dealer gonna get an x-mas present when I take it in after x-mas and say fix it...$$$ OUCH  $$$.<P>Ahh well...enough ranting.. thanks all.<BR>At least My "Little Duce Coupe" has NEVER let me down.<P>------------------<BR>Little Duce Coupe<BR>"You Don't Know What She Costs"||||reg||8
